    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d856">

                <pb facs="0916" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg796"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 45.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of a note from the Japanese
                    minister at this capital, asking the use of your good offices for the release of
                    three Japanese merchants captured in the northern part of Korea about May,
                        1904.<anchor n="c" xml:id="d856-f1"/> Their names are said to be Nobe
                    Ichitaro, Yagabe Chiuzaburo, and Gyo, the son of the latter.</p>
                <p>The Department desires you to comply with the minister’s request.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D.
                    Peirce.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
